cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the archived samples, please cite the thesis (see preferred-citation)."
title: "molewhacker-newtrinos"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Reindel
    given-names: Valentin
    email: valentin.reindel@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Technical University of Munich, Department of Physics"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/valeagent/molewhacker-newtrinos"
abstract: >-
  Application of the MoleWhacker adaptive importance sampler to a real
  physics likelihood: a joint three-flavor fit of the neutrino-oscillation
  experiments Daya Bay, KamLAND and MINOS (11 parameters, both mass
  orderings) with the likelihoods of Newtrinos.jl, benchmarked against
  Metropolis-Hastings, NUTS, nested sampling and plain importance sampling
  under a common likelihood-evaluation budget, and its extension by the
  IceCube DeepCore atmospheric sample to 24 parameters.
preferred-citation:
  type: thesis
  title: "Importance Sampling Methods in the Bayesian Analysis Toolkit"
  authors:
